\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The determinant derivative behind the link current}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{TauCeti's \leanref/tauceti{Matrix.fderiv_det_apply} supplies
#{D\det(Q)[B]=\det(Q)\operatorname{tr}(Q^{-1}B)} over a complete
nontrivially normed field when #{\det Q} is a unit. For the
positive Hermitian operator of \ref{fdip-0074}, complex positive
definiteness supplies invertibility. In the ordered vertex basis
named in that proof, the derivative is the matrix with entries
#{-iU_e} at #{(h,s)} and #{i\overline{U_e}} at #{(s,h)}. The
logarithm, angle direction, current sign and Gaussian expectation
are the additional steps in the proposition. The formal declaration
does not state this current law.}
